<Solution>
  <!--
    The paths leave the repository, and that is not an accident. Since the
    submodules came out of libs/, XMPPConsole.csproj reaches sideways for
    ..\..\Ratatoskr, Ratatoskr for ..\..\Hermod and Hermod for ..\..\Styx, so
    the only tree in which this builds at all is the four checked out beside
    each other:

        XMPPConsole/   Ratatoskr/   Hermod/   Styx/

    A solution that stopped at the repository boundary would therefore be a
    solution that does not open. What is gained by naming the three anyway is
    what the sibling solutions gain: they build and step through as source
    rather than as a reference that resolves to somewhere off-screen.

    Their test suites are deliberately not here. Elsewhere in the family -
    XMPPConformanceTests, TCPEchoTestClient - the dependencies are pinned
    submodules, so running HermodTests or RatatoskrTests from that solution
    measures the revision that checkout pins. Here they would be master, and a
    red run would not say whether the console or something upstream had moved.
    The protocol's suite lives with Ratatoskr and has a gate of its own; this
    solution answers for the console.
  -->
  <Folder Name="/Dependencies/">
    <Project Path="../Ratatoskr/Ratatoskr/Ratatoskr.csproj" />
    <Project Path="../Hermod/Hermod/Hermod.csproj" />
    <Project Path="../Styx/Styx/Styx.csproj" />
  </Folder>
  <Project Path="XMPPConsole/XMPPConsole.csproj" />
  <Project Path="XMPPConsole.Tests/XMPPConsole.Tests.csproj" />
</Solution>
